RunInfo: 'Run on pp QCD-instanton, minimum-bias, multijet, W+jets, or ttbar samples. Histograms with finite positive integrals are normalized to unit area, as in the Section 4 shape comparisons. Counters provide the denominator and selection numerators for efficiencies within the events delivered to Rivet and cannot include generator or shower attempts rejected beforehand.'
Beams: [p+, p+]
Energies: [[6500, 6500]]
Description:
  'Particle-level implementation of the indicative QCD instanton observables in
   Section 4 of Khoze, Krauss and Schott, arXiv:1911.09726. Charged tracks with
   pT > 0.5 GeV and |eta| < 2.5 approximate reconstructed tracks, and anti-kT
   R = 0.4 particle jets with pT > 20 GeV and |eta| < 4.5 approximate reconstructed
   particle jets. The analysis forms reconstructed instanton-mass proxies from
   the selected tracks and jets, then fills track observables in the low-mass
   region and jet observables in the high-mass region. Sphericity is evaluated
   after boosting the selected track or jet system to its reconstructed rest frame.'
ValidationInfo:
  'UNVALIDATED: this is a particle-level analysis derived from the published
   Section 4 description, not a Delphes reproduction of the original plots.
   Validate by comparing normalized shapes for QCD-instanton and background
   samples against Figs. 8-11 of arXiv:1911.09726.'
Keywords:
 - QCD instantons
 - soft bombs
 - event shapes
 - multiplicity
 - sphericity
